# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages redirects
#
# A page's canonical address is the CLEAN one — /compress-image, never
# /compress-image.html. Netlify answers both forms with a 200, so without the
# rule at the bottom of this file every page would have two live URLs and
# would split its own link equity between them. First match wins, so the two
# specific rules above the wildcard do.

/index.html   /   301

# Defensive: the other common spelling of the same file.
/index.htm    /   301

# Search Console fetches this exact filename and nothing else, so it must
# never be redirected by the wildcard below. If you rotate the token in
# site.config.json, update this line too — npm run verify will tell you.
#/googleK8OpKzoXFUM-vUMqgWfSAmUMmkRy07k0pbBtiAIMuhM.html   /googleK8OpKzoXFUM-vUMqgWfSAmUMmkRy07k0pbBtiAIMuhM.html   200

# Everything else: the .html form 301s onto the canonical clean URL.
/*.html   /:splat   301
